      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T16:59:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "85597f56_e9114660",
      "revId": "a9916dfab537740cb9a7bf4aa258003130410ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0843a892_6485a827",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/ConfigurationFlags.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1312909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-06T20:18:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can Sink/Source Audio location of PAC record be provided to Vendor module so that it can make right decision for Vendor config in case it opt to choose using this flag. I see places where channel count is being passed but not channel locations any reason for doing so?",
      "revId": "a9916dfab537740cb9a7bf4aa258003130410ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a288b195_6f2ecbda",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/ConfigurationFlags.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-07T10:15:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Channel count is provided so the vendor lib knows if Bluetooth request a configuration for 1 or more channels in single CIS.\n\nAllocation is handled by Bluetooth stack.",
      "parentUuid": "0843a892_6485a827",
      "revId": "a9916dfab537740cb9a7bf4aa258003130410ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "883829bf_9931cc03",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/ConfigurationFlags.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1312909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T19:20:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am talking about condition where Vendor codec/module actually make use willing to set Audio Channel Allocation (not Bluetooth Stack) which this flag is meant for I believe vendor(non-standard) codec then Sink/Source Audio location PAC should also be made available (along-with Source/Sink PAC records) so that vendor module can send it to Bluetooth Stack.",
      "parentUuid": "a288b195_6f2ecbda",
      "revId": "a9916dfab537740cb9a7bf4aa258003130410ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "198772d7_ae70ea96",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/audio/ConfigurationFlags.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1928988
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T13:35:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems that BT stack can just pass the Audio Channel Allocation as part of the requirements. This way the BT stack has the control over the audio channel allocations (and this is what we want), but the vendor module still has a chance to return different configuration for each allocation as now we return a List\u003cAseConfiguration\u003e for each direction and audio locations are part of the requirements.\n\nThe flag does not seem helpful at all, since the BT stack wants the control over the allocations, and it will not add them anyway when the vendor specific and opaque configuration byte array is used. I just removed it.\n\nPlease let me know if you see any problem with this mechanism.",
      "parentUuid": "883829bf_9931cc03",
      "revId": "a9916dfab537740cb9a7bf4aa258003130410ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
